  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "CodeMender",
          "version": "dev"
        }
      },
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "IMPROPER NEUTRALIZATION OF SPECIAL ELEMENTS USED IN AN SQL COMMAND ('SQL INJECTION')",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "SQL Injection in User Search Endpoint: The endpoint `/api/user/search` extracts the `username` parameter directly from query parameters without sanitization and formats it into a raw SQL query string via an f-string. This string is then executed using `cursor.execute()`, leading to SQL injection.\n\n- Source: `username = request.args.get('username', '')` (line 65)\n- Sanitization/Validation: None. The user input is formatted directly into the SQL query string.\n- Sink: `cursor.execute(query)` (line 72)\n\nConceptual Exploit Payload:\nSend an HTTP GET request with a SQL injection payload in the `username` query parameter:\n```http\nGET /api/user/search?username=' UNION SELECT id, username, email, role FROM users WHERE '1'='1"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 70,
                  "endLine": 72
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "IMPROPER NEUTRALIZATION OF SPECIAL ELEMENTS USED IN AN OS COMMAND ('OS COMMAND INJECTION')",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "OS Command Injection in Ping Tool Endpoint: The endpoint `/api/tools/ping` takes untrusted JSON input `host` from the request body and constructs a shell command string using string interpolation (`f\"ping -c 1 {host}\"`), passing it directly to `os.system()`. This allows arbitrary OS command execution with the privileges of the web application process.\n\n- Source: `host = data.get('host', '')` from `request.get_json()` (lines 106-107)\n- Sanitization/Validation: Only checks `if not host:`. No validation or sanitization against command injection metacharacters (e.g. `;`, `&`, `|`, `` ` ``, `$()`).\n- Sink: `os.system(command)` (line 114)\n\nConceptual Exploit Payload:\nSend an HTTP POST request containing command chaining operators:\n```http\nPOST /api/tools/ping HTTP/1.1\nHost: localhost:5000\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{\n  \"host\": \"127.0.0.1; id\"\n}\n```\nThe shell executes `ping -c 1 127.0.0.1; id`, running the injected command `id` on the host operating system."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 113,
                  "endLine": 114
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "SQL Injection in User Search Endpoint: The endpoint `/api/user/search` extracts the `username` parameter directly from query parameters without sanitization and formats it into a raw SQL query string via an f-string. This string is then executed using `cursor.execute()`, leading to SQL injection.\n\n- Source: `username = request.args.get('username', '')` (line 65)\n- Sanitization/Validation: None. The user input is formatted directly into the SQL query string.\n- Sink: `cursor.execute(query)` (line 72)\n\nConceptual Exploit Payload:\nSend an HTTP GET request with a SQL injection payload in the `username` query parameter:\n```http\nGET /api/user/search?username=' UNION SELECT id, username, email, role FROM users WHERE '1'='1"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
